---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ContactCta from "../components/ContactCta.astro";

const aboutJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "ProfilePage",
  "@id": "https://maurizioturatti.com/about/#profile",
  url: "https://maurizioturatti.com/about/",
  name: "About Maurizio Turatti",
  description:
    "Twenty-five years of making technical decisions and living with the consequences. Architecture advice grounded in direct experience building and operating software.",
  mainEntity: {
    "@type": "Person",
    name: "Maurizio Turatti",
    url: "https://maurizioturatti.com/",
    jobTitle: "Architecture Advisor and Company Co-Founder",
    worksFor: {
      "@type": "Organization",
      name: "SoftInstigate",
      url: "https://restheart.org",
    },
    alumniOf: {
      "@type": "EducationalOrganization",
      name: "Università degli Studi di Milano",
    },
  },
};
---

<Base
  title="About - Maurizio Turatti"
  description="Twenty-five years of making technical decisions and living with the results. Architecture advisory grounded in direct experience building and operating software."
  ogImage="/images/og-image.png"
  jsonLd={aboutJsonLd}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/markdown" href="/Maurizio_Turatti_CV.md" title="Maurizio Turatti CV (Markdown)" />
    <meta name="keywords" content="Maurizio Turatti, architecture advisor, technical due diligence, CTO advisory, architectural decisions, software architecture" />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="hero hero--first">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="hero-headline">The decisions behind the systems.</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="page-content section-stack">
    <div class="section-block">
      <div class="section-body section-body--lead section-body--spacious">
        <p>
          I have spent twenty-five years making technical decisions and living with the consequences, often under incomplete information and unclear constraints. Understand the problem, surface the trade-offs that actually matter, and make the call that keeps risk manageable. The trade-offs that matter are the ones that show up at 2 AM when something breaks in production.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most architecture problems are decision problems that were never made explicit.
        </p>
        <p>
          Co-founder of <a href="https://softinstigate.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >SoftInstigate</a
          > and creator of <a href="https://restheart.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RESTHeart</a>, in production for 10+ years.
        </p>
        <div style="display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:12px; margin-top:16px;">
          <a href="/Maurizio_Turatti_CV.md" download="Maurizio_Turatti_CV.md" class="cta-btn cta-btn--primary">Download CV (Markdown)</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- How I work -->
    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">How I work</h2>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <div class="surface-card">
          <p class="card-label">Unclear systems and constraints</p>
          <p class="card-text">
            My work usually starts where the problem is not yet fully defined.
            Requirements are incomplete, constraints are implicit, and the
            system is already running in production. The first task is
            understanding what actually matters before proposing anything.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="surface-card">
          <p class="card-label">Decisions under pressure</p>
          <p class="card-text">
            Most systems do not fail at design time. They fail when
            assumptions meet production reality. The decisions that matter
            are the ones made with incomplete information, where the
            consequences of being wrong are visible and expensive.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="surface-card">
          <p class="card-label">Long-term consequences</p>
          <p class="card-text">
            Architecture decisions are difficult to undo. A choice that
            saves a month now can cost a year later. Every decision I make
            considers how the system will need to evolve, and how hard it
            will be to change course if the original assumptions were wrong.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">AI and architecture</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          AI amplifies architectural decisions. It increases the value of
          good structure and the cost of accumulated technical debt. The
          decision is where it creates value in this specific system, and
          what the architecture needs to support it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Open source</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/SoftInstigate/restheart"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"><strong>RESTHeart</strong></a
          >: Agent-ready backend for MongoDB<br />
          <a
            href="https://github.com/SoftInstigate/facet"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"><strong>Facet</strong></a
          >: Data-driven web framework: turn APIs into HTML, zero code<br />
          <a
            href="https://github.com/SoftInstigate/ermes-mail"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"><strong>Ermes Mail</strong></a
          >: Async e-mail library and CLI for Java<br />
          <a href="https://github.com/mkjsix" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >All projects on GitHub →</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Writing</h2>
      <div class="section-body">
        <p>
          <a href="/writing/the-system-is-working"
            ><strong>The system is working. That is the problem.</strong></a
          >
          (Jun 2026)<br />
          <a
            href="https://medium.com/softinstigate-team/facet-a-different-approach-to-web-development-af884abe0b69"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            ><strong>Facet: A Different Approach to Web Development</strong></a
          >
          (Jan 2026)<br />
          <a
            href="https://medium.com/softinstigate-team/mongodb-deprecates-data-api-and-https-endpoints-how-restheart-can-help-58ea0c44660d"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            ><strong>MongoDB Deprecates Data API: How RESTHeart Can Help</strong></a
          >
          (Feb 2025)
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ContactCta subtext="info@maurizioturatti.com" />
</Base>
